  "question": {
    "text": "A solution of a metal ion when treated with $\\mathrm{KI}$ gives a red precipitate which dissolved in excess KI to give a colourless solution. Moreover, the solution of metal ion on treatment with a solution of cobalt (II) thiocyanate gives rise to a deep blue crystalline precipitqte. The metal ion is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "266i8",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{Pb}^{2+}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SLBmn",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{Hg}^{2+}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "61lhQ",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nv5qt",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{Co}^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{Hg}^{2+}+2 \\mathrm{I}^{-} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{HgI}_2, \\mathrm{HgI}_2+\\mathrm{H}^{-} \\\\\n& \\text {(Excess) }\\left.\\longrightarrow \\mathrm{HgI}_4\\right]^{2-} \\\\\n& \\text { Soluble }^{2-} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{Hg}^{2+}+\\mathrm{Co}(\\mathrm{SCN})_2 \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{Hg}(\\mathrm{SCN})_2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBlue crystalline ppt.",
